### 5. Plinko Game Engine

#### [NEW] `src/components/PlinkoGame.tsx`

A canvas-based Plinko simulation using **Matter.js** physics:

- **Board**: 8 rows of pegs, 9 slots at bottom
- **Multipliers**: `[0.5×, 0.8×, 1×, 1.5×, 2×, 1.5×, 1×, 0.8×, 0.5×]` (symmetric — center slots are more likely but pay less; edge slots are rare but pay 5× or 10×)
- Alternative high-variance config: `[10×, 5×, 2×, 1×, 0.5×, 1×, 2×, 5×, 10×]`
- **Animation**: Ball drops from random x-offset at top, bounces through pegs, lands in ~2-3 seconds
- **Server authority**: Multiplier is pre-determined server-side via cryptographic RNG (`crypto.getRandomValues`). Client animation is cosmetic only — the ball is guided to land in the predetermined slot.
- **Visual**: Dark card with neon-colored pegs, glowing ball, slot labels with multiplier values

#### [NEW] `src/app/api/plinko/route.ts` — Server-side multiplier generation

Weighted random distribution:
| Multiplier | Weight | Probability |
|-----------|--------|-------------|
| 0.5× | 25 | 25% |
| 0.8× | 20 | 20% |
| 1× | 20 | 20% |
| 1.5× | 15 | 15% |
| 2× | 10 | 10% |
| 5× | 7 | 7% |
| 10× | 3 | 3% |

